<!--{ or01 : rich }-->
# 10. Organising

Comments for your colleagues, hidden lines for the machinery, the text of a
document, and its files and folders. About six minutes.
<!--{ or02 : rich }-->
## Comments

A comment is a note on a line. It is stored in the document, inside the line
it is about, and moves with it. The right margin shows how many comments a
line has: the next line has one. Click the number to read it in the comments
pane; **Alt+C** shows or hides the pane.

To write a comment, edit a line and press **Shift+F2**. In rich text a small
field opens: type your note and press **Enter**, then **Ctrl+Enter**. Start a
comment with your name, so that others know who wrote it.
<!--{ or03 : markdown }-->
The span and the loads come from the client's brief.
<!--[ Ada: rev. B of the brief, received on 2026-11-02. ]-->
<!--{ or04 : rich }-->
## Hidden lines

Lines can be hidden, as rows in Excel: a line with intermediate steps, or one
the reader does not need. A hidden line stays in the document and still
computes. Select lines, open the commands (**F1**) and choose **Hide the
selected cells**. The line numbers skip hidden lines, and a double rule shows
where they are. **Unhide the cells in the selection** brings them back:
select the lines above and below the double rule first.

Every lesson has a hidden line at its top, which imports the small library
that checks your exercises. **Show or hide the hidden cells** shows it,
greyed out.

## The text of a document

**Alt+U** shows the text the document is saved as, read-only. Every line of
the sheet starts there with a marker, which holds the line's name and type,
and its comments are written inside it. Press **Alt+U** again to go back. The text is all there is: a document
is a plain text file, which any text editor can open.
<!--{ or05 : rich }-->
## Files and folders

The navigation pane shows the documents of the folder. Right-click a
document, a folder or the empty area of the pane for its commands.

**Your turn.**

1. Right-click the empty area below the documents in the navigation pane
   and choose **New folder…**. Name it `practice`.
2. Right-click the folder `practice` and choose **New document…** (or press
   **Alt+N**). Name it `notes`: the new document opens.
3. In `notes`, write two lines. Add a comment to the first one.
4. Hide the second one.
5. Save with **Ctrl+S**, and come back here with the browser's back button.
<!--{ or06 : formula }-->
<% texl.import "practice/notes.texl" ~> (notes -> tutorial.check (type notes.source == "Text")) %>
<!--{ or07 : formula }-->
<% texl.import "practice/notes.texl" ~> (notes -> tutorial.check ((type notes.source == "Text") ? (text.find ("<!-" + "-[") notes.source >= 0))) %>
<!--{ or08 : formula }-->
<% texl.import "practice/notes.texl" ~> (notes -> tutorial.check ((type notes.source == "Text") ? (text.find "| hidden" notes.source >= 0))) %>
<!--{ or09 : markdown }-->
The checks read `practice/notes.texl`: they show ✓ Done once the document
exists, has a comment, and has a hidden line.

| Command | What it does |
|---------|--------------|
| **Rename** (F2) | Changes the name of a document or folder |
| **Move to…** | Moves it to another folder |
| **Duplicate** | Copies a document next to it, under a new name |
| **Copy link** | Copies its address, for a link or an import (lesson 8) |
| **Delete** | Moves it to a hidden `.trash` folder: nothing is erased |

Links do not follow: after a rename or a move, links and imports in other
documents that point to the old name stop working, and Stilo warns you.

More in the manual: [Comments](https://www.onlabs.org/manual/editor/comments.html),
[Hide lines](https://www.onlabs.org/manual/editor/lines.html#hide-lines) and
[Files and folders](https://www.onlabs.org/manual/editor/files.html).
